      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 3.39,
          "en": "Instructor: Now, I guess it makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.39,
          "end": 5.64,
          "en": "to start with saving recipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.64,
          "end": 8.73,
          "en": "because it's hard to fetch them if we never save them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.73,
          "end": 11.82,
          "en": "And for that, I will add a new method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.82,
          "end": 13.8,
          "en": "to the data storage service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.8,
          "end": 16.86,
          "en": "which I'll name storeRecipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.86,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "Now of course you can name this method however you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 24.03,
          "en": "And now here we got two possible routes we could take.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.03,
          "end": 27.21,
          "en": "We could accept the recipes we want to store here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.21,
          "end": 30.03,
          "en": "as an argument by injecting our or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.03,
          "end": 32.73,
          "en": "by importing our recipe model up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.73,
          "end": 35.79,
          "en": "And then defining that this should be of type recipe array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.79,
          "end": 38.43,
          "en": "And then here we could just write the HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.43,
          "end": 40.38,
          "en": "where we want to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.38,
          "end": 43.26,
          "en": "well store these recipes on the back end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 46.653,
          "en": "by sending some meaningful request to some URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.49,
          "end": 48.75,
          "en": "Now we could do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.75,
          "end": 53.4,
          "en": "We could also inject the recipes service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.4,
          "end": 55.98,
          "en": "into our data storage service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.98,
          "end": 57.21,
          "en": "That would be the other way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.21,
          "end": 60.72,
          "en": "And then we could directly get our currently loaded recipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.72,
          "end": 62.16,
          "en": "from that recipe service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.16,
          "end": 64.32,
          "en": "And we avoid this extra argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.32,
          "end": 66.45,
          "en": "And that is what I will do indeed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.45,
          "end": 69.21000000000001,
          "en": "So I will inject the number service here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.21000000000001,
          "end": 73.86,
          "en": "the recipes service, which is of type recipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.86,
          "end": 75.15,
          "en": "recipe service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.15,
          "end": 77.16,
          "en": "let's name it recipeService here too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.16,
          "end": 78.48,
          "en": "You need to add that import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.48,
          "end": 80.85,
          "en": "to the recipe service, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 80.85,
          "end": 82.68,
          "en": "And now with that, inject it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 82.68,
          "end": 84.81,
          "en": "I get my recipes by reaching out to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.81,
          "end": 89.81,
          "en": "this.recipeService and by simply getting the recipes with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.06,
          "end": 91.71000000000001,
          "en": "getRecipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 91.71000000000001,
          "end": 93.404,
          "en": "So this retrieves our list of recipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 93.404,
          "end": 97.22999999999999,
          "en": "which are now temporarily stored in that constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.22999999999999,
          "end": 99.36,
          "en": "Therefore, we can remove that model import up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.36,
          "end": 101.91,
          "en": "We don't need it because we're not using the type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.91,
          "end": 104.85,
          "en": "And now with the recipes loaded here in store recipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 104.85,
          "end": 107.16,
          "en": "we can make our HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 107.16,
          "end": 110.61,
          "en": "So here we can now use the Angular HTTP client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.61,
          "end": 113.13,
          "en": "And now we could definitely make a post request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.13,
          "end": 115.74000000000001,
          "en": "if you would want to add one recipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 115.74000000000001,
          "end": 118.17,
          "en": "But I want to store all my recipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 118.17,
          "end": 119.003,
          "en": "and I essentially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 119.003,
          "end": 122.37,
          "en": "want to override any previous recipes I stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 122.37,
          "end": 124.8,
          "en": "And for that Firebase gives us an endpoint,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 124.8,
          "end": 127.23,
          "en": "which we read by using a put request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 127.23,
          "end": 130.65,
          "en": "And again, that strongly depends on the API you're using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.65,
          "end": 131.483,
          "en": "on the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 131.483,
          "end": 135.15,
          "en": "Here, Firebase works such that we can send a put request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 135.15,
          "end": 138.32999999999998,
          "en": "to a specific URL to override all the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 138.32999999999998,
          "end": 140.01,
          "en": "that is stored under that node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 140.01,
          "end": 142.17000000000002,
          "en": "Your backend might work differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 142.17000000000002,
          "end": 143.7,
          "en": "if you are creating your own backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 143.7,
          "end": 145.23,
          "en": "it might be working differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 145.23,
          "end": 148.74,
          "en": "It's always depending on the API you're working with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 148.74,
          "end": 152.19,
          "en": "But Firebase works such that if we send a port request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 152.19,
          "end": 153.48,
          "en": "to a URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 153.48,
          "end": 156.06,
          "en": "any data that's in there will be overwritten.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 156.06,
          "end": 160.26,
          "en": "So let me copy that here, that URL, let's add it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 160.26,
          "end": 162.21,
          "en": "That's the URL I wanna send this to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 162.21,
          "end": 164.55,
          "en": "though that's not the entire URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 164.55,
          "end": 168.06,
          "en": "Instead, it should be sent to /recipes.json.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 168.06,
          "end": 170.64,
          "en": "The .json is a Firebase characteristic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 170.64,
          "end": 173.16,
          "en": "You need to add this at the end of the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 173.16,
          "end": 175.2,
          "en": "It has nothing to do with the data you were sending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 175.2,
          "end": 178.32,
          "en": "or with Angular and well slash recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 178.32,
          "end": 180.93,
          "en": "That's just how the Firebase real time database works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 180.93,
          "end": 183.66,
          "en": "It gives us a REST API where we in the end define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 183.66,
          "end": 187.62,
          "en": "our own nodes which will then be translated to folders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 187.62,
          "end": 190.65,
          "en": "You could say where the data will be stored in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 190.65,
          "end": 192.24,
          "en": "So now we're sending a put request there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 192.24,
          "end": 195.63,
          "en": "but a put request just like a post request needs data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 195.63,
          "end": 196.463,
          "en": "to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 196.463,
          "end": 199.75,
          "en": "we need to tell Angular what to put on this URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 200.85,
          "end": 203.07,
          "en": "to say or what to attach to this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 203.07,
          "end": 206.16,
          "en": "And that will be our recipes here, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 206.16,
          "end": 207.41,
          "en": "I guess that makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 208.38,
          "end": 209.49,
          "en": "Now, as you learn,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 209.49,
          "end": 213.12,
          "en": "this alone will not send the HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 213.12,
          "end": 215.49,
          "en": "Instead, that request will only be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 215.49,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "as soon as we subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 220.74,
          "en": "Now we got two routes you could take here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 220.74,
          "end": 223.137,
          "en": "We can return our observable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 223.137,
          "end": 225.21,
          "en": "by adding the return keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 225.21,
          "end": 228.12,
          "en": "and then we can subscribe in the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 228.12,
          "end": 230.88,
          "en": "where we're calling store recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 230.88,
          "end": 233.933,
          "en": "Now, in our case here, that will be the header component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 233.933,
          "end": 236.57999999999998,
          "en": "because that is where our buttons are.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 236.57999999999998,
          "end": 237.413,
          "en": "And in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 237.413,
          "end": 240.93,
          "en": "I'm not interested in subscribing in that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 240.93,
          "end": 244.17,
          "en": "because I don't wanna show a loading spinner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 244.17,
          "end": 245.46,
          "en": "though of course you could do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 245.46,
          "end": 247.59,
          "en": "But here, I just don't want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 247.59,
          "end": 249.03,
          "en": "and therefore there is no need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 249.03,
          "end": 250.89,
          "en": "for me to subscribe in the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 250.89,
          "end": 253.23,
          "en": "because the component in this scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 253.23,
          "end": 256.53,
          "en": "will not be interested in whether that request is done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 256.53,
          "end": 257.363,
          "en": "or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 257.363,
          "end": 259.5,
          "en": "If that's different in your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 259.5,
          "end": 261.15,
          "en": "obviously you can use the pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 261.15,
          "end": 264.48,
          "en": "I also showed you in the last section where you do subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 264.48,
          "end": 268.2,
          "en": "in the component that triggered that request or that method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 268.2,
          "end": 270.84,
          "en": "So here instead, I will subscribe directly in the service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 270.84,
          "end": 274.62,
          "en": "because I have no interest in the response in my component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 274.62,
          "end": 277.5,
          "en": "And I will get back a response here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 277.5,
          "end": 280.986,
          "en": "and we can console.log that to have a look at it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 280.986,
          "end": 284.22,
          "en": "I will not do much else with it though here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 284.22,
          "end": 285.87,
          "en": "Now with that, we just need to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 285.87,
          "end": 288.81,
          "en": "that the store recipes method is getting called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 288.81,
          "end": 289.65,
          "en": "And as I mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 289.65,
          "end": 292.8,
          "en": "that will happen from inside the header component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 292.8,
          "end": 295.32,
          "en": "There we have that save data button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 295.32,
          "end": 297.18,
          "en": "Let's add a click listener here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 297.18,
          "end": 299.28,
          "en": "and maybe call onSaveData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 299.28,
          "end": 301.74,
          "en": "or whatever you want to call that method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 301.74,
          "end": 304.56,
          "en": "And then let's add that method to the header component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 304.56,
          "end": 305.393,
          "en": "And in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 305.393,
          "end": 308.7,
          "en": "we now have to call our newly added safe recipes method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 308.7,
          "end": 310.83,
          "en": "in this data storage service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 310.83,
          "end": 312.3,
          "en": "And for that of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 312.3,
          "end": 316.59,
          "en": "we need to inject our data storage service here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 316.59,
          "end": 317.853,
          "en": "by using its type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 318.99,
          "end": 323.52,
          "en": "Make sure you import that type from your file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 323.52,
          "end": 327.03,
          "en": "from your data storage service file in the shared folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 327.03,
          "end": 330.33,
          "en": "And now with it injected in on safe data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 330.33,
          "end": 333.93,
          "en": "we can use the data storage service and call store recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 333.93,
          "end": 335.613,
          "en": "And that should already be all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 336.93,
          "end": 338.82,
          "en": "Now let's go back to our application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 338.82,
          "end": 340.44,
          "en": "which should have reloaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 340.44,
          "end": 343.59000000000003,
          "en": "And let's click Manage, Safe Data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 343.59000000000003,
          "end": 346.14,
          "en": "Here I'm getting back a response that looks promising.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 346.14,
          "end": 347.79,
          "en": "So basically, Firebase in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
